":[\"All Sectors\"],\"heading\":\"Sectors\"},{\"links\":[\"Setting up Business\",\"List of Clearances\",\"Know Your Clearances\",\"Exports\",\"Policy \u0026 Notifications\",\"Country Desk\",\"User Manual\"],\"heading\":\"Business in Tamil Nadu\"},{\"links\":[\"Non-Resident Tamil Investment Promotion Division\"],\"heading\":\"NRT IP Division\"},{\"links\":[\"Media Gallery\",\"e-Newsletters\",\"Blogs\"],\"heading\":\"Media \u0026 Events\"},{\"links\":[\"BIU\",\"Industrial Park Walk through\"],\"heading\":\"Initiatives\"},{\"links\":[\"FAQs\",\"Submit Your Queries\",\"Contact Us\"],\"heading\":\"Help \u0026 Support\"}],\"copyright\":\"© 2025 All rights reserved\",\"subscribe\":\"Subscribe\",\"bottomLinks\":[\"Privacy Policy\",\"Terms of Use\",\"Disclaimer\",\"Site Map\"],\"visitorCount\":\"Visitor Count: 104281692\",\"subscribePlaceholder\":\"Enter your email address\"}}],\"initialLang\":\"en\",\"children\":\"$L14\"}]]}]}],\"$L15\",\"$L16\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5:[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{\"pageData\":{\"id\":855,\"pageName\":\"districts\",\"slug\":\"districts\",\"langCode\":\"en\",\"status\":\"Published\",\"response\":{\"seo\":{\"meta_title\":\"Districts | Guidance Tamil Nadu\",\"meta_description\":\"Discover investment opportunities across Tamil Nadu's 38 districts. Explore localized industrial hubs, sector-specific advantages, infrastructure, and regional economic insights for strategic business expansion.\",\"meta_keywords\":\"Tamil Nadu districts, invest in Tamil Nadu regions, industrial hubs Tamil Nadu, Chennai investment, Coimbatore manufacturing, Madurai business opportunities, Hosur electronics hub, Tamil Nadu regional infrastructure, district-wise investment, Guidance Tamil Nadu districts\"},\"title\":\"Explore Tamil Nadu\",\"description\":\"Tamil Nadu's commitment to business has led to a sturdy public infrastructure in the areas of connectivity, water, power, and telecom among others. This has ensured the intact supply chains and channels, and development of human and social capital in line with the rapidly evolving economic landscape.\",\"allDistrictsSection\":{\"title\":\"All Districts\",\"description\":\"Tamil Nadu is unique in the way that there is equitable development across all districts. For administrative conveniences, the state has been segmented into 38 districts. Every district is distinctive in its own features and specialties while also permeated with the intrinsic local culture.\"},\"actionButtons\":[{\"icon\":\"https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/128/6057/6057141.png\",\"alt\":\"Tourist attractions\",\"action\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/district-map-purple.jpg\"},{\"icon\":\"https://cdn-icons-png.flaticon.com/128/2642/2642502.png\",\"alt\":\"Map location\",\"action\":\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Tamil+Nadu/@10.8099323,75.647429,7z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x3b00c582b1189633:0x559475cc463361f0!8m2!3d11.1271225!4d78.6568942!16zL20vMDdjOTg?entry=ttu\u0026g_ep=EgoyMDI1MTIwMS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D\"}],\"groupColors\":[\"rgba(196, 184, 233, 1)\",\"rgba(147, 129, 200, 1)\",\"rgba(106, 86, 161, 1)\"],\"groups\":{\"group1\":[\"Nagapattinam\",\"Thiruvarur\",\"Mayiladuthurai\",\"Thanjavur\",\"Ariyalur\",\"Pudukkottai\",\"Kallakurichi\",\"Cuddalore\",\"Perambalur\",\"Villupuram\",\"Tiruvannamalai\",\"Tirunelveli\",\"Thoothukudi\",\"Tenkasi\",\"Virudhunagar\",\"Ramanathapuram\",\"Theni\",\"Sivagangai\",\"Madurai\",\"Dindigul\",\"Dharmapuri\",\"Kanyakumari\"],\"group2\":[\"Salem\",\"Ranipet\",\"Vellore\",\"Tirupattur\",\"Krishnagiri\",\"Karur\",\"Tiruppur\",\"Coimbatore\",\"Nilgiris\",\"Erode\",\"Namakkal\",\"Tiruchirapalli\"],\"group3\":[\"Tiruvallur\",\"Chennai\",\"Kancheepuram\",\"Chengalpattu\"]},\"districts\":{\"Nagapattinam\":{\"id\":\"District 1\",\"title\":\"Nagapattinam\",\"description\":\"Nagapattinam is a coastal district of Tamil Nadu known for its fishing and tourism industry. Agriculture and allied sector is still the major means of livelihood for the people of this district. It is bounded by the Bay of Bengal in the east, Palk Strait in the south, Tiruvarur district in the west and Puducherry district in the north. It was from this seaport city many trade embassies were sent to eastern world in medieval and later periods. Vedaranyam salt swamp that runs along the coast from Point Calimere is said to be the longest swamp of its kind in the state.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-nagapattinam.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"2715.83 sq km\",\"Population\":\"1,616,450\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"83.59%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\"},{\"label\":\"Nagapattinam Railway Station\"}],\"details\":{\"title\":\"Nagapattinam\",\"heroTitle\":\"Nagapattinam has what it takes for your Business to Flourish\",\"websiteButton\":\"Go to Nagapattinam District Website\",\"heroImage\":\"https://investingintamilnadu.com/DIGIGOV/themes/tnswp/images/prelogin-pages-images/district-img/nagapattinam/nagapattinam.png\",\"description\":[\"Nagapattinam is a coastal district of Tamil Nadu known for its fishing and tourism industry. Agriculture and allied sector is still the major means of livelihood for the people of this district. It is bounded by the Bay of Bengal in the east, Palk Strait in the south, Tiruvarur district in the west and Puducherry district in the north. It was from this seaport city many trade embassies were sent to eastern world in medieval and later periods. Vedaranyam salt swamp that runs along the coast from Point Calimere is said to be the longest swamp of its kind in the state.\"],\"stats\":{\"area\":\"2715.83 sq km\",\"population\":\"16,16,450 (Based on 2011 census)\",\"populationDensity\":\"595 per sq km\",\"sexRatio\":\"1025 (Females to 1000 Males)\",\"literacyRate\":\"83.59%\",\"temperature\":\"19.3°C to 40.6°C\"},\"resources\":{\"title\":\"Reliable Resources\",\"forestCover\":\"The district has a total forest cover of 198 sq. km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with sandy coastal alluvium soil.\",\"water\":\"The rivers cauvery, vennar barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like crude oil, natural gas, quartz, limestone, heavy mineral sand, titanium and lignite.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\",\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\",\"Nagapattinam Railway Station\",\"150 Kms Total Network of State \u0026 National Highways\",\"150 Kms Total Railway Track Length\"],\"industries\":[\"Fishing\",\"Tourism\",\"Agriculture\"],\"education\":{\"description\":\"The district has wide spread and well-developed ecosystem of Educational Institutes and facilities.\",\"institutions\":{\"generalArtsAndScienceColleges\":14,\"industrialTrainingInstitute\":11,\"engineeringCollege\":8,\"nursingColleges\":2,\"universities\":2,\"medicalCollege\":1,\"agriculturalCollege\":1,\"hotelManagementInstitute\":1}},\"companies\":[],\"expert\":{\"name\":\"Rajavel P\",\"email\":\"rajavel@investtn.in\"}}},\"Thiruvarur\":{\"id\":\"District 2\",\"title\":\"Thiruvarur\",\"description\":\"Rice-bowl district with religious heritage.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-tiruvarur.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"2161 sq km\",\"Population\":\"12,64,277\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"82.86%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\"},{\"label\":\"Tiruvarur Railway Station\"}],\"details\":{\"title\":\"Thiruvarur\",\"heroTitle\":\"Thiruvarur has what it takes for your Business to Flourish\",\"websiteButton\":\"Go to Thiruvarur District Website\",\"heroImage\":\"https://investingintamilnadu.com/DIGIGOV/themes/tnswp/images/prelogin-pages-images/district-img/thiruvarur/thiruvarur.png\",\"description\":[\"Thiruvarur was one of the five traditional capitals during the Chola empire and forms the part of the rice bowl of Tamil Nadu. It is bounded by Nagapattinam district on the east, Mayiladuthurai district on the north, Thanjavur district on the west, Palk Strait on the south and a small border on the northeast with the Karaikal district of the union territory Puducherry. The industrial units here are spread across the district and is mainly confined to agro-based industries. The extraction of natural gas and power generation plants have been setup in the recent years.\"],\"stats\":{\"area\":\"2161 sq km\",\"population\":\"12,64,277 (Based on 2011 census)\",\"populationDensity\":\"585 per sq km\",\"sexRatio\":\"1017 (Females to 1000 Males)\",\"literacyRate\":\"82.86%\",\"temperature\":\"22.60°C to 39.70°C\"},\"resources\":{\"title\":\"Reliable Resources\",\"forestCover\":\"The district has a total forest cover of 59 sq. km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with red soil and sandy coastal alluvium.\",\"water\":\"The rivers vennar, vettar and bamini barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like lignite, quartz and garnet.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\",\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\",\"Tiruvarur Railway Station\",\"456 Kms Total Network of State \u0026 National Highways\",\"67 Kms Total Railway Track Length\"],\"industries\":[\"Rice mills\",\"Groundnut Products\",\"Coir Processing\"],\"education\":{\"description\":\"The district has wide spread and well-developed ecosystem of Educational Institutes and facilities.\",\"institutions\":{\"artsAndScienceColleges\":11,\"polytechnicColleges\":4,\"engineeringColleges\":2,\"medicalCollege\":1}},\"companies\":[],\"expert\":{\"name\":\"Rajavel P\",\"email\":\"rajavel@investtn.in\"}}},\"Mayiladuthurai\":{\"id\":\"District 3\",\"title\":\"Mayiladuthurai\",\"description\":\"Mayidauthurai is the newest district formed through the bifurcation of Nagapattinam district in December 2020. It is bounded by Cuddalore district on the north, Thanjavur district on the west, Karaikal district of the Union territory of Pondicherry to the south, Tiruvarur district to the south west and Bay of Bengal on the east. The coastal district is primarily involved in fishing and agriculture. There are remains of the Dutch settlements in the state in Tharangambadi taluk. The district falls into the famous religious trail with temples attributed to major hindu gods are found here.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-mayiladuthurai.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"1172 sq km\",\"Population\":\"918,356\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"78.78%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\"},{\"label\":\"Mayiladuthurai Railway Station\"}],\"details\":{\"title\":\"Mayiladuthurai\",\"heroTitle\":\"Mayiladuthurai has what it takes for your Business to Flourish\",\"websiteButton\":\"Go to Mayiladuthurai District Website\",\"heroImage\":\"https://investingintamilnadu.com/DIGIGOV/themes/tnswp/images/prelogin-pages-images/district-img/mayiladuthurai/mayiladuthurai.png\",\"description\":[\"Mayiladuthurai is the newest district formed through the bifurcation of Nagapattinam district in December 2020. It is bounded by Cuddalore district on the north, Thanjavur district on the west, Karaikal district of the Union territory of Pondicherry to the south, Tiruvarur district to the south west and Bay of Bengal on the east. The coastal district is primarily involved in fishing and agriculture. There are remains of the Dutch settlements in the state in Tharangambadi taluk. The district falls into the famous religious trail with temples attributed to major hindu gods are found here.\"],\"stats\":{\"area\":\"1172 sq km\",\"population\":\"9,18,356 (Based on 2011 census)\",\"populationDensity\":\"782 per sq km\",\"sexRatio\":\"1024 (Females to 1000 Males)\",\"literacyRate\":\"78.78%\",\"temperature\":\"32.8°C to 39.4°C\"},\"resources\":{\"title\":\"Reliable Resources\",\"forestCover\":\"The district has a total forest cover of 198* sq. km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with sandy coastal alluvium soil and black soil.\",\"water\":\"The rivers cauvery barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like crude oil, natural gas, quartz, limestone, heavy mineral sand, titanium and lignite.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\",\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\",\"Mayiladuthurai Railway Station\",\"150* Kms Total Network of State \u0026 National Highways\",\"150* Kms Total Railway Track Length\"],\"industries\":[\"Fishing\",\"Agriculture\"],\"education\":{\"description\":\"The district has wide spread and well-developed ecosystem of Educational Institutes and facilities.\",\"institutions\":{\"generalArtsAndScienceColleges\":6,\"polytechnicColleges\":5,\"nursingColleges\":2,\"teacherTrainingInstitution\":1,\"hotelManagementCollege\":1,\"engineeringCollege\":1}},\"companies\":[],\"expert\":{\"name\":\"Rajavel P\",\"email\":\"rajavel@investtn.in\"}}},\"Thanjavur\":{\"id\":\"District 4\",\"title\":\"Thanjavur\",\"description\":\"Thanjavur popularly known as 'the granary of south India' is bound by river Coloroon on the north which separates it from Ariyalur and Tiruchirapalli district, Thiruvarur and Nagapattinam districts in the east, Palk Strait and Pudukottai in the south and Pudukottai in the west. It is one of the largest paddy cultivation region in south India. It is also famous for rural artefacts such as the 'Thanjavur Doll', 'Thanjavur painting' and unique musical instruments that are high in demand in the international market.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-thanjavur.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"3396.57 sq km\",\"Population\":\"2,405,890\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"82.64%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\"},{\"label\":\"Thanjavur Railway Station\"}],\"details\":{\"title\":\"Thanjavur\",\"heroTitle\":\"Thanjavur has what it takes for your Business to Flourish\",\"websiteButton\":\"Go to Thanjavur District Website\",\"heroImage\":\"https://investingintamilnadu.com/DIGIGOV/themes/tnswp/images/prelogin-pages-images/district-img/thanjavur/thanjavur.png\",\"description\":[\"Thanjavur popularly known as 'the granary of south India' is bound by river Coloroon on the north which separates it from Ariyalur and Tiruchirapalli district, Thiruvarur and Nagapattinam districts in the east, Palk Strait and Pudukottai in the south and Pudukottai in the west. It is one of the largest paddy cultivation region in south India. It is also famous for rural artefacts such as the 'Thanjavur Doll', 'Thanjavur painting' and unique musical instruments that are high in demand in the international market.\"],\"stats\":{\"area\":\"3396.57 sq km\",\"population\":\"24,05,890 (Based on 2011 census)\",\"populationDensity\":\"708 per sq km\",\"sexRatio\":\"1035 (Females to 1000 Males)\",\"literacyRate\":\"82.64%\",\"temperature\":\"22.1°C to 36.5°C\"},\"resources\":{\"title\":\"Reliable Resources\",\"forestCover\":\"The district has a total forest cover of 436 sq. km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with red soil, clay soil and sandy alluvial.\",\"water\":\"The rivers cauvery barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like garnet and lignite.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\",\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\",\"Thanjavur Railway Station\",\"265 Kms Total Network of State \u0026 National Highways\",\"200 Kms Total Railway Track Length\"],\"industries\":[\"Stainless Steel\",\"Brass Metals Product\",\"Silk weaving\",\"Bronze icon making\",\"Coir Processing\",\"Rice mills\"],\"education\":{\"description\":\"The district has wide spread and well-developed ecosystem of Educational Institutes and facilities.\",\"institutions\":{\"artsAndScienceColleges\":32,\"engineeringColleges\":15,\"polytechnicColleges\":14,\"universities\":4}},\"companies\":[],\"expert\":{\"name\":\"Rajavel P\",\"email\":\"rajavel@investtn.in\"}}},\"Ariyalur\":{\"id\":\"District 5\",\"title\":\"Ariyalur\",\"description\":\"Ariaylur district with rich mineral deposits of Celeste, Limestone, Shale, Sandstone, Canker and Phosphate nodules are famous for its cement industry. It is bounded by Cuddalore district in the north, Thanjavur district in the south, Perambalur \u0026 Trichy districts in the west and Mayiladuthurai district in the east. over 59 percent of the workforce in the district is employed in the agriculture and allied sector. Ariyalur also houses large number of food processing units in its industrial complex.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-ariyalur.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"1940 sq km\",\"Population\":\"754,894\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"71.34%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Trichy International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Chennai Port \u0026 Cuddalore Port\"},{\"label\":\"Ariyalur Railway Station\"}],\"details\":{\"title\":\"Ariyalur\",\"heroTitle\":\"Ariyalur has what it takes for your Business to Flourish\",\"websiteButton\":\"Go to Ariyalur District Website\",\"heroImage\":\"https://investingintamilnadu.com/DIGIGOV/themes/tnswp/images/prelogin-pages-images/district-img/ariyalur/ariyalur.png\",\"description\":[\"Ariyalur district with rich mineral deposits of Celeste, Limestone, Shale, Sandstone, Canker and Phosphate nodules are famous for its cement industry. It is bounded by Cuddalore district in the north, Thanjavur district in the south, Perambalur \u0026 Trichy districts in the west and Mayiladuthurai district in the east. Over 59 percent of the workforce in the district is employed in the agriculture and allied sector. Ariyalur also houses large number of food processing units in its industrial complex.\"],\"stats\":{\"area\":\"1940 sq km\",\"population\":\"7,54,894 (Based on 2011 census)\",\"populationDensity\":\"389 per sq km\",\"sexRatio\":\"1015 (Females to 1000 Males)\",\"literacyRate\":\"71.34%\",\"temperature\":\"24.3°C to 35.2°C\"},\"resources\":{\"title\":\"Reliable Resources\",\"forestCover\":\"The district has a total forest cover of 329 sq. km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with red soil and black soil.\",\"water\":\"The rivers kollidam and vellar barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like lignite, celeste, limestone, shale, sandstone and fire clay.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Trichy International Airport\",\"Chennai Port \u0026 Cuddalore Port\",\"Ariyalur Railway Station\",\"29.17 Kms Total Network of State \u0026 National Highways\",\"75 Kms Total Railway Track Length\"],\"industries\":[\"Cement\",\"Food Processing\"],\"education\":{\"description\":\"The district has wide spread and well-developed ecosystem of Educational Institutes and facilities.\",\"institutions\":{\"engineeringColleges\":3,\"generalArtsScienceColleges\":2,\"polytechnicColleges\":2}},\"companies\":[],\"expert\":{\"name\":\"Rajavel P\",\"email\":\"rajavel@investtn.in\"}}},\"Pudukkottai\":{\"id\":\"District 6\",\"title\":\"Pudukkottai\",\"description\":\"As one of the princely states of Tamil Nadu, Pudukottai holds rich cultural heritage with fortresses, palaces, temples, cave paintings and many other historical monuments. It is well endowed with natural resources of land and sea bounded by the marine hedge of Bay of Bengal in the east conjoined by the southern districts viz, Trichy, Sivagangai, Ramanathapuram and Thanjavur. The district has three major industrial estates at Machuvadi, Mathur and Vallanur.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-pudukkottai.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"4663 sq km\",\"Population\":\"1,618,345\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"77.19%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Cuddalore Port \u0026 Thoothukudi Port\"},{\"label\":\"Pudukkottai Railway Station\"}]},\"Tiruchirapalli\":{\"id\":\"District 7\",\"title\":\"Tiruchirapalli\",\"description\":\"Tiruchirappalli is a place of historic, cultural and economic importance. It is one of the five nodal centres of the announced Defence Industrial Corridors. The district is known for the presence of major Public Sector Undertakings, such as the Bharat Heavy Electricals Limited, Heavy Alloy Penetrator Project and the Ordnance Factory. It takes pride in having prestigious educational institutions such as NIT, IIM, and IIIT among others. The district is bounded in the north by Salem and Namakkal in the east by Perambalur, Ariyalur and Thanjavur in the south by Pudukottai, in the west by Karur.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-tiruchirappalli.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"4407 sq km\",\"Population\":\"2,722,290\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"83.23%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Chennai Port \u0026 Cuddalore Port\"},{\"label\":\"Tiruchirappalli Railway Station\"}]},\"Kallakurichi\":{\"id\":\"District 8\",\"title\":\"Kallakurichi\",\"description\":\"Kallakurichi also known as the 'Home of Agriculture' houses cluster of rice processing units. It is surrounded by Viluppuram district in the east and Cuddalore and Perambalur in the south, Salem in the west and by Thiruvannamalai and Dharmapuri district in the north. Textiles, Jewellery and agricultural feeds are also major businesses here.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-kallakurichi.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"3520.37 sq km\",\"Population\":\"1,370,281\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"63.49%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Chennai International Airport\"},{\"label\":\"Chennai Port \u0026 Cuddalore Port\"},{\"label\":\"Chinnaselam Railway Station\"}],\"details\":{\"title\":\"Kallakurichi\",\"heroTitle\":\"Kallakurichi has what it takes for your Business to Flourish\",\"websiteButton\":\"Go to Kallakurichi District Website\",\"heroImage\":\"https://investingintamilnadu.com/DIGIGOV/themes/tnswp/images/prelogin-pages-images/district-img/kallakurichi/kallakurichi.png\",\"description\":[\"Kallakurichi also known as the 'Home of Agriculture' houses cluster of rice processing units. It is surrounded by Viluppuram district in the east and Cuddalore and Perambalur in the south, Salem in the west and by Thiruvannamalai and Dharmapuri district in the north. Textiles, Jewellery and agricultural feeds are also major businesses here.\"],\"stats\":{\"area\":\"3520.37 sq km\",\"population\":\"13,70,281 (Based on 2011 census)\",\"populationDensity\":\"389 per sq km\",\"sexRatio\":\"984 (Females to 1000 Males)\",\"literacyRate\":\"63.49%\",\"temperature\":\"21°C to 38°C\"},\"resources\":{\"title\":\"Reliable Resources\",\"forestCover\":\"The district has a total forest cover of 853* sq. km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with red soil and black soil.\",\"water\":\"The rivers gomukhi , manimuktha, mayura and gadilam barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like quartz, rough stone, river sand, black granite, red earth, copper, lead-zinc, silver, iron ore, china clay, limestone and fire clay.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Chennai International Airport\",\"Chennai Port \u0026 Cuddalore