 km\",\"soil\":\"The area is predominantly covered with black soil ,calcareous soil, alluvial soil, ferruginous soil and sandy loamy.\",\"water\":\"The rivers vellar barrages are used to irrigate the land.\",\"naturalResources\":\"The region is rich in natural reserves like fire clay, gypsum, limestone, quartz and barytes.\"},\"resourcesImage\":\"/invest-innovate/invest-innovate-bg.png\",\"infrastructure\":[\"Salem Domestic Airport\",\"Chennai Port \u0026 Cuddalore Port\",\"Ariyalur Railway Station\",\"39.4 Kms Total Network of State \u0026 National Highways\",\"30 Kms Total Railway Track Length\"],\"industries\":[\"Agriculture\",\"Manufacturing\"],\"education\":{\"description\":\"The district has wide spread and well-developed ecosystem of Educational Institutes and facilities.\",\"institutions\":{\"polytechnicColleges\":6,\"medicalColleges\":4,\"engineeringColleges\":3,\"bEdColleges\":2,\"generalArtsScienceColleges\":2,\"governmentCollege\":1,\"agricultureCollege\":1}},\"companies\":[],\"expert\":{\"name\":\"Rajavel P\",\"email\":\"rajavel@investtn.in\"}}},\"Villupuram\":{\"id\":\"District 11\",\"title\":\"Villupuram\",\"description\":\"Viluppuram known as the 'Sugar Bowl of Tamil Nadu' has an array of agro-based industries, rice mills and sugar mills. The district has the largest rural population of 2.9 million in the state. It shares its borders with Bay of Bengal and the union Territory of Pondicherry in the east, Kancheepuram and Tiruvannamalai districts in the north, Cuddalore and Perambalur districts in the south and Dharmapuri and Salem districts in the west. Auroville, an experimental township, has around 170 social enterprises providing employment to around 5,000 people from the surrounding villages.\",\"image\":\"https://storage.investingintamilnadu.com/Guidance/Uploads/Photos/tn-viluppuram.svg\",\"stats\":{\"Area\":\"3725.54 sq km\",\"Population\":\"3,458,873\",\"Literacy Rate\":\"71.88%\"},\"iconLabels\":[{\"label\":\"Chennai International Airport\"},{